{"name":"Broccoli & Stilton soup","permalink":"broccoli-stilton-soup","edit":"https://github.com/The-Silverwood-Institute/Recibase/tree/master/src/main/scala/se/reciba/api/recibase/recipes/BroccoliStiltonSoup.scala","source":null,"description":"A rich and nutritious winter warmer","tagline":null,"notes":["The original recipe uses a 1:2 stilton to broccoli ratio rather than our decadent 1:1 ratio. If you'd prefer not to get gout then stick with the original ratio."],"dated_notes":[{"date":"2022-07-07","note":"Doubled the sauce"}],"tags":["Cold Weather","Slow","Vegetarian","Scales","Soup","Low Effort","Freezes","Better Next Day"],"inherited_tags":["Vegetarian-ish","Pescatarian"],"image":null,"ingredients_blocks":[{"name":null,"ingredients":[{"name":"Broccoli","quantity":"2 heads","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Stilton","quantity":"220g","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Onion","quantity":"1 onion","prep":"roughly chopped","notes":null},{"name":"Garlic","quantity":"3 cloves","prep":"diced","notes":null},{"name":"Stock Cube","quantity":"1","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Boiled water","quantity":"1L","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Butter","quantity":"1 knob","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Ground Nutmeg","quantity":null,"prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Lemon Juice","quantity":null,"prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Salt","quantity":null,"prep":null,"notes":null}]}],"method":["Cut off the broccoli florets and chop the stalk into 2cm pieces.","Heat a large pan over a medium heat then melt the knob of butter.","Add the garlic and onions then soften for a few minutes.","Add the broccoli stalks and cook for another minute.","Add the broccoli florets, stock cube and enough water to cover all but the last inch of the mixture.","Add a few drops of lemon juice and a small sprinkle of nutmeg.","Bring to the boil then cover and simmer for 20 minutes.","Roughly chop the stilton.","Turn off the heat and blend.","Put back over a low heat and add the stilton. Stir until melted. Be careful: the mixture will now stick more easily and possibly spit.","Add more lemon juice and possibly salt to taste.","Serve with fresh bread."]}